(1794822, 241342, 30049, '<td valign="top">Simile defined: <i>A figure of speech in which two essentially unlike things are explicitly compared, usually by means of <u>like</u> or <u>as</u>, ...</i> <br/> <br/>To say this is a simile was reaching a bit and putting extra words out there that didn''t exist, IMO.  ;^)<br/> <br/>Quite honestly, ''stubborn as a nail'' never crossed my mind.  ''Bent out of shape'' did.  Stubborn in this case (single word) was meant to portray the human trait of stubbornness (or creating a personification) in that the nail was being stubborn - not wanting to go into the wood - resisting...<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Caltrop:</b></div><hr/><i> ''stubborn as a nail'' is a simile not a personification. sorry<br/> <br/>Edit - In looking back on my comment it seems a bit harsh - I did not mean it to be quite so. I do get the feel of the pic and it is a good shot. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Simile defined: A figure of speech in which two essentially unlike things are explicitly compared, usually by means of like or as, ...  To say this is a simile was reaching a bit and putting extra words out there that didn''t exist, IMO.  ;^) Quite honestly, ''stubborn as a nail'' never crossed my mind.  ''Bent out of shape'' did.  Stubborn in this case (single word) was meant to portray the human trait of stubbornness (or creating a personification) in that the nail was being stubborn - not wanting to go into the wood - resisting... Originally posted by Caltrop: ''stubborn as a nail'' is a simile not a personification. sorry Edit - In looking back on my comment it seems a bit harsh - I did not mean it to be quite so. I do get the feel of the pic and it is a good shot. ', '2005-10-19 05:55:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1794824, 241342, 30049, '<td valign="top">Who are "they"?  What were YOU looking for?  I''m guessing that you felt this didn''t meet the challenge as a Personification?  In what way?  I''m not trying to be spiteful, just trying to encourange something a little more tangible.  Sounds like you are commenting based on what others think you should say and not what you think personally.  ;^)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tmorninglory96:</b></div><hr/><i> Funny, but not quite what I think they wanted! </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Who are "they"?  What were YOU looking for?  I''m guessing that you felt this didn''t meet the challenge as a Personification?  In what way?  I''m not trying to be spiteful, just trying to encourange something a little more tangible.  Sounds like you are commenting based on what others think you should say and not what you think personally.  ;^) Originally posted by tmorninglory96: Funny, but not quite what I think they wanted! ', '2005-10-19 06:00:15.000000', NULL, 0),
