(1805813, 242107, 42995, '<td valign="top">77ltd, they were normal 120v bulbs.  the wires were all attached in parallel and then attached to an extension cord with built-in lamp dimmer.<br/> <br/>check out a view of the wiring <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=246166" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a>.  i doubt it would meet electrical code!<br/> <br/>i never ran the lights at anything close to full brightness, though, and only for a few seconds at that.  they were very, very dim during the exposure.<br/></td>', '77ltd, they were normal 120v bulbs.  the wires were all attached in parallel and then attached to an extension cord with built-in lamp dimmer. check out a view of the wiring here.  i doubt it would meet electrical code! i never ran the lights at anything close to full brightness, though, and only for a few seconds at that.  they were very, very dim during the exposure.', '2005-10-23 22:43:56.000000', NULL, 0),
